Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 13 CLINICAL DATA  74 y o  female with breast carcinoma by fine needle aspiration undergoing right modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVASING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 7 OF 8 LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY SOFT TISSUE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SPECIMEN  1   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 5 OF 5 LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY VEINS  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tissue fragment with a 0 8cm firm lymph node  The node is sectioned to reveal a white tan  firm cut surface  Half the node is frozen as FX 1  and saved frozen  The remainder is submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  additional axillary nodes  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of adipose tissue from which lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes B through C  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  right modified radical mastectomy   is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x 22 x 4 5cm  with an attached axilla of  14 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0 cm and an overlying skin ellipse measuring  23 x 11cm   containing an eccentric nipple  4 0cm in diameter  7 7cm away from the medial end of the skin ellipse  The nipple areola complex is grossly unremarkable  No scars are grossly identified in the overlying skin ellipse  The deep resection margin consist of a smooth fascial plane  The specimen is inked black and the axillary contents are removed  A lymph node dissection is performed  The main mastectomy specimen is then serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  gritty area with a stellate border that comes to within 0 8cm of the deep  closest  margin  The inferior margin is 2 0cm away  and the superior margin is 2 5cm away from the mass  SECTION CODE  D L  Axillary lymph nodes  M  Mass  in relation to deep margin  N  Closest inferior margin  O  Deep margin  P Q  Representative sections of tumor nodules  R  Representative section of normal breast parenchyma away from mass lesion  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS 1  LYMPH NODE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART B  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    EXCISION   report_end  , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 53 CLINICAL DATA  Large lobular carcinoma with lobular carcinoma in situ on outside biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA FORMING SEVERAL SMALL NODULES BOTH ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND AWAY FROM IT  IN SITU CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The in situ carcinoma exhibits a mixture of ductal and lobular characteristics  The invasive carcinoma forms several seemingly discrete nodules  making the size of the infiltrating component impossible to determine  The largest focus measures 0 4cm  and together the foci probably aggregate to about 1 0cm  Blood vessl and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  The tumor in the axillary lymph node spans about 0 3cm in greatest dimension in tissue section  and the cells extend into axillary fat  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number only is an 805 gram modified radical mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with an axillary tail REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm  At the central aspect of the inferior skin margin is a 2 5cm areola and nipple  and a healing scar is present 2 0cm in length extending to within 0 8cm to the superior margin and beginning 8 0cm from the medial margin of the skin ellipse  The specimen is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy cavity extending to within 0 7cm of the deep margin and to within 0 4cm of the superior margin  The remaining breast is unremarkable  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  A 0 5cm  hard  well circumscribed nodule is identified 3 0cm deep to the nipple  Section code  A D  biopsy site with deep margin E  biopsy site with superior margin F J  representative breast tissue K  well circumscribed nodule L  nipple M O  axillary lymph nodes Res