rner  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 99 at 10 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number   l breast and axillary contents  is a 19 x 17 x 2 3cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 10 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail  and REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ellipse of nipple bearing skin  There is a short stitch on a superior aspect and a long stitch on the lateral aspect of the specimen  The skin contains no focal lesions  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm round grey tan hard mass with poorly defined edges that is 2cm from the posterior and inferior margins  Adjacent to this  the parenchyma contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm irregular area with multiple firm nodules which comes to 1 2cm from the posterior margin  2 5cm away from the main mass there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area that also contains multiple firm nodules  and this comes to 1 3cm from the inferior margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is notable for other small areas of nodularity  The mass is entirely submitted in A D with the closest posterior margin in C  Representative sections of the adjacent nodular area and the closest anterior margin are submitted in E  Representative sections of the other large nodular area are submitted in F  Representative sections of small nodular areas in the parenchyma are submitted in G I  with an inferior margin in G and a posterior margin in I  The lymph nodes from the axillary tail are submitted in J L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number   additional axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm irregular fragment as adipose tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  focally hemorrhagic lymph node the node is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette M  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Jaime A Rivera 