Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 38 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer on FNA outside hospital  reviewed at MGH                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO THE POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT AND FOCALLY TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTERIOR  SUPERIOR  AND MEDIAL MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  UNREMARKABLE FAT  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY NODES   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  A FEW TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 20     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  number and  left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE lumpectomy specimen  inked as follows  black deep end superficial  red superior  medial green  lateral blue  inferior yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm white mass grossly abutting the superficial and deep margins  Tumor and adjacent superficial margin are frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Tumor and adjacent deep margin is frozen as FX 2  FX 2 is submitted in cassette A  Section Code  B  tumor with superficial  deep and inferior yellow margin  superficial and is fatty   C  Anterior and deep tissue   superficial fatty   D  Tumor  superior  E  most lateral tissue  radial  F  Most medial tissue  radial  G  firm tissue  inferior  Labeled  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE in aggregate mass of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  submitted in cassettes H L  Labeled  additional left axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate mass of adipose tissue and tiny lymph nodes measuring less than 0 3cm each  Tissue submitted entirely in cassettes M N  Labeled  left breas