ssette A  The remaining nodule is in cassette B and the rest of the specimen is in cassettes C through F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm fragment of firm  rubbery breast tissue a long stitch marking the lateral margin and a short stitch marking the superior margin  The posterior surface of the specimen is inked yellow on black  The superior surface orange on black and the inferior surface red on black  The anterior  medial  and lateral surfaces are inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal pink tan  rubbery cut surface with focal cystic changes  Further sectioning of specimen reveals a firm  rubbery  white tan  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  5cm nodule with white tan nodular cut surface which is present away from the white fibrous tissue in fat in the anterior aspect of the specimen and grossly abuts the anterior resection margin  SECTION CODE G  Lateral resection margin  en face section  H  Representative section of firm  white  rubbery tissue with adjacent superior and posterior resection margin  I  Representative section of firm  white  rubbery tissue with adjacent posterior and inferior resection margin  J  Representative section of firm  white  rubbery tissue with adjacent anterior resection margin  K L  Representative section of separate nodule in anterior fat  M Q  Additional representative section of specimen showing focally white  firm solid and focally cystic cut surface  R  Medial resection margin  en face section  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   BIOPSY  FIBROADENOMA WITH FOCAL DCIS  O R  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCIS