a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal breast tissue composed of approximately 70  fibrous tissue and 30  adipose tissue  A metal clip is identified in the fibrous tissue  located 0 7cm from the superior margin  and more than 2cm from the remaining margins  The area immediately surrounding the metal clip is grossly unremarkable and soft  The remaining fibrous tissue contains an ill defined area which is slightly more firm than the surrounding parenchyma  This area measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 2 5cm  It focally abuts the inferior and anterior margins  The firm areas are 0 5cm from the closest superior margin  0 5cm from the closest lateral margin  and more than 1cm from the remaining margins  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area surrounding the clip and its relationship to the superior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the firm area and its relationship to the inferior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the firm area and its relationship to the anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the firm area and its relationship to the lateral margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the firm area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections  to include tissue in superior aspect where the clip was located in the latter sections  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm portion of adipose tissue  Upon dissection  multiple nodular tan gray rubbery lymph nodes are identified  they range from REMOVED_DATE to 4 2cm in greatest dimension  They are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node