uch clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a right mastectomy specimen measuring 22 x 18 x 4 5cm with a 12 x 5cm grossly unremarkable ellipse of skin containing a 2 x 2cm grossly unremarkable nipple areolar complex  Also included is a 7 x 4 x 1 8cm axillary content  The deep margin is inked and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm moderately well circumscribed  firm  gray nodular mass in the medial half of the specimen  this mass is 0 8cm from the deep margin which is the closest margin and more than 4cm from all the other margins  Also noted medially  1 5cm from the large nodular mass  is a 0 8cm irregular  stellate  hard white tan nodular lesion located at 2 5cm from the medial margin and 0 7cm from the deep margin  which is the closest margin   The remainder of the breast is adipose with large gray white  firm  irregular areas  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Larger mass with deep margin  B  Larger mass with deep margin  C D  Smaller mass with deep margin  E F  Representative sections from the tissue adjacent to the larger mass  G  Representative section from the medial half of the breast  H I  Representative sections from the lateral half of the breast  J  Nipple  The axillary tail contains ten lymph nodes varying from REMOVED_DATE to 0 8cm  The most proximal lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes K and L  The most distal lymph nodes are submitted in cassette M  Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Checked.
