utinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm irregular piece of tan yellow tissue containing REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm firm nodule which abuts a resection margin  Sectioning reveals the nodule as being well demarcated with a lobular surface  A portion of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  a piece of tissue is taken for electron microscopy  and the remainder of the tumor is submitted in A through D  with additional representative tissue in E through J  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA    NEUROENDOCRINE  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION    report_end  , Unchecked.
