 underestimate the true size of the tumor  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  C  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL TISSUE   EXCISION  1  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  D  SKIN  LEFT MASTECTOMY FLAP   EXCISION  SKIN AND SUB CUTIS WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED   E  SKIN  RIGHT MASTECTOMY FLAP   EXCISION  SKIN AND SUB CUTIS WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED   By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 5 containers  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a 21 x 20 x 3 5cm skin sparing simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm nipple areolar complex with a grossly unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm nipple  The specimen is oriented as follows by the surgeon  A suture indicates 12 o clock  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal fibrous breast parenchyma with areas of nodularity and multiple cysts up to 0 5cm in diameter  from which clear straw colored fluid is expressed  No focal lesions or abnormalities are identified  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the posterior portion of the specimen  including black inked posterior margin   