Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 55 CLINICAL DATA  56 year old white female with a left breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH MARKED CHRONIC INFLAMMATORY AND REPARATIVE REACTION WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION AND FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ADIPOSE TISSUE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 20 OF 20 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 43                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are three separate specimens  Labeled  Left breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm breast re excision specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm overlying skin ellipse containing a 2 5cm well healed  central scar  A short stitch marks superior  long stitch marks lateral  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 2 5cm diameter biopsy cavity  1 4cm below the skin ellipse  filled with yellow  serous fluid  The wall of the cyst is light tan with focal hemorrhagic areas  and cross section of the cyst reveals chaulky  yellow fat necrosis immediately beneath the cavity lining  extending up to the overlying skin ellipse  There is no gross evidence of residual carcinoma  The biopsy cavity comes to within 0 2cm of the closest superior an inked resection margin  0 5cm from the closest deep inked margin  0 5cm from the closest inferior inked margin  0 5cm from the closest lateral inked margin  and greater than 1cm from the closest medial inked margin  SECTION CODE  A  closest margin  superior  B  skin and biopsy cavity  C E  representative section of biopsy cavity  Labeled  Left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm fibrofatty axillary node dissection containing approximately eighteen nodules  0 2cm in diameter to 1 0cm in diameter  All nodules are soft to focally firm  and tan pink  submitted in F through K  Labeled  Left additional axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of adipose tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm ill defined thickening in the adipose tissue  entirely in L  SECTION CODE  A  closest margin of biopsy cavity  superior  B  skin and biopsy cavity  C E  representative sections of biopsy cavity  F K  axillary lymph nodes  L  tissue from additional axillary contents  M Q  additional sections of biopsy cavity  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION PART B  ADIPOSE TISSUE LEFT AXILLA  EXCISION    report_end  , Checked.
