is a localization wire in place  inserting within the anterior aspect  The superior aspect is inked black  the inferior blue  the medial green and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a cut surface consisting of yellow lobulated adipose tissue and white dense fibrous tissue  No lesions or masses are identified  The specimen is submitted sequentially from anterior to posterior in its entirety in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the anterior most section in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and an area of possible calcification in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Dennis Sgroi M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Dennis Sgroi M D   on REMOVED_DATE Proofread by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
