Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  12 MAY 95 at 12 32 CLINICAL DATA  BCS                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION   1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  75   AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  AND WITH FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  25    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  WITH FOCAL COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  Microcalcifications are associated with the carcinoma  Fragmentation of the biopsy precludes optimal assessment of tumor size  The tumor in one fragment is 1 9cm and in the other fragment the smallest tumor dimension is 0 6cm  thus the tumor is at least 2 5cm  The tumor is present in seven of eight slides  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  17 MAY 95 at 15 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 95 at 08 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  are two fragments of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  The longer fragment contains a needle guide wire and is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm irregular well demarcated firm nodule with infiltrative borders  the nodule abuts the ink  A representative section is frozen as FX 1  Frozen section is saved and sent to Cox 5  Remainder of longer specimen is entirely submitted in A through F  nodule in B through E  The smaller fragment is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular well demarcated yellow firm nodule with infiltrative borders grossly abutting the ink  No frozen is done  submitted entirely in G through H  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Keith Thomas Paige M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  Kimberly Christa Sippel  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS LESION , Checked.
