Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 28 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal mammogram   calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  FIBROSIS  ATROPHY  AND CYST FORMATION  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  90   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN IN SMALL FOCI  AND INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  AND EXTENDING TO MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  CALCIFIED FIBROADENOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 18     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy   needle loc    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm white pink breast tissue with localizing wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal predominantly white breast parenchyma  No area grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma  No frozen section done  Submitted entirely in A through J with area near tip of wire in B and C  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy   needle loc    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of firm  yellow pink breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm nodule  a fine stellate white tissue with hemorrhagic streaks and calcifications near localizing wire  The nodule reaches the margin in multiple points  A section is frozen as FX 1  Submitted entirely in K through P  Frozen saved for Cox 5  Tissue submitted for Dr  Sgroi  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS ONLY   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis b