Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  08 MAY 98 at 15 08 CLINICAL DATA  Clinical history not given                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  NOTE  All examined inked margins are negative  A focus of possible lymphatic invasion is seen  No blood vessel or perineural invasion is seen  BREAST  SUPERIOR LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  13 MAY 98 at 16 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast excision specimen  with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm skin ellipse with 1 knot designating the lateral margin and 2 knots designating the superior margin  The breast is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a tan  firm  stellate mass  measuring 1 9cm in greatest dimension  grossly coming to within 0 4cm from the closest superior and inferior margins  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A B  Tumor in relation to closest superior margin  C D  Tumor in relation to closest inferior margin  E   Representative section of uninvolved breast tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior lateral margin   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  with punctate areas of hemorrhage  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in Cassettes F L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fat  dissected through the multiple grossly unremarkable lymph nodes  Representative sections of the lymph nodes are submitted in Cassettes M P  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SUPERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCES