Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 44 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE II III  95   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5     SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is situated 1 5cm from the closest deep margin and measures 2cm in maximum diameter  Perineural invasion is identified  however  no vascular invasion is seen  Twelve of twelve lymph nodes are negative for tumor  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  NOTE  There is tumor present within 1 millimeter of the resection margin  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 47 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 37     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  NEGATIVE  progesterone receptor  213 fm mg cytosolic protein  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 39     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 36     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal multiple firm areas  measuring REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm in size consistent with cysts  No frozen section performed  Firm areas submitted in A through E and the remainder of the tissue in D through J  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labe